at="epo"><addressbook><name>YANAGIHARA HIROKAZU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>DAINIPPON INK AND CHEMICALS, INC.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKATSU, HARUYOSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKEUCHI, KIYOFUMI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YANAGIHARA, HIROKAZU</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKATSU HARUYOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKEUCHI KIYOFUMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YANAGIHARA HIROKAZU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKATSU, HARUYOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKEUCHI, KIYOFUMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YANAGIHARA, HIROKAZU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A nematic liquid crystal composition characterized in that the liquid crystal composition comprises a compound represented by any of general formulae (I-1) to (I-5) which have naphthalene-2,6-diyl, decahydronaphthalene-2,6-diyl or 1,2,3,4-tetrahydronaphthalene-2,6-diyl; and a liquid crystal display using the same.  This nematic liquid crystal composition allows the extension of the operation temperature range for a liquid crystal display characteristic through, for example, its improvement in compatibility and in storage stability at a low temperature, permits the reduction of driving voltage and the improvement of its change with temperature and enables achieving a relatively fast response for a given driving voltage, and accordingly is extremely suitable for use in TN, STN, TFT, IPS, MVA, OCB, ECB, PC, PNLC, PDLC, PSCT or the like.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une composition de cristaux liquides nématiques qui renferme un composé représenté par l'une des formules générales (I-1) à (I-5) contenant naphtalène-2,6-diyle, décahydronaphtalène-2,6-diyle, ou 1,2,3,4-tétrahydronaphtalène-2,6-diyle. L'invention concerne également un écran à cristaux liquides utilisant cette composition. Cette composition de cristaux liquides nématiques permet d'augmenter la plage de température de fonctionnement d'un écran à cristaux liquides, par exemple par une amélioration de sa compatibilité et de sa stabilité au stockage, d'une réduction de sa tension de commande, et d'une amélioration de son changement à la température, facilitant ainsi l'obtention d'une réponse relativement rapide pour une tension de commande donnée. Cette composition est donc particulièrement apte à être utilisée dans TN, STN, TFT, IPS, MVA, OCB, ECB, PC, PNLC, PDLC, PSCT, ou similaire.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>